# Ribstrand: a kart circuit on a grey northern coast, after Ribshore.
# Units in metres: x east, z south, from the world's north-west corner.
# The sea is to the west. The lap runs south down the wet beach, turns
# inland through winding dunes, comes back north over a run of jumps across
# the dune crests, and drops back onto the beach, where the last straight
# runs south down the middle of a giant's ribcage to the line.
track ribstrand size 768 style shore
title RIBSTRAND
blurb A fast lap of a grey northern coast: half a kilometre of wet beach at the water's edge under the sea stacks, a tangle of small bends through the dunes past the bones of a giant's calf, three jumps over the dune crests, and back down the beach through the middle of a titan's ribcage to the line.
race laps 3 rivals 5 vehicle kart
road 14.5 bank 1.25
land 30 1.5
hour 11
lights 25

# The beach: a bench just over high water, rising to the dunes over 45 m.
plateau 27 45 -10,-10 240,-10 232,150 236,250 244,400 238,500 228,600 230,700 240,778 -10,778
# The sea floor, falling away past the waterline (sea level 26).
plateau 13 75 -10,-10 112,-10 104,150 108,250 116,400 110,500 100,600 102,700 112,778 -10,778
# The dunes rise inland toward the east.
